Give the DFlash and DFlash2 speculators per-request top-k / top-p under CUDA
graphs.

SamplingStates hands out its values from a rotating UVA pool, so the .gpu
tensor is not a capture-stable pointer, and apply_staged_writes rotates those
tensor objects on every engine step. The eager input-preparation kernel stages
the current values into persistent device buffers, which the captured graph
then reads; the owner is kept rather than the rotating tensors.

